<title>NETHERLANDS: CSM jumps after U.S. acquisition news.</title>
<headline>CSM jumps after U.S. acquisition news.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Dutch food group CSM NV stood out on a generally firmer Amsterdam bourse on Friday, rising sharply following news of a U.S. acquisition.</p>
<p>At 0844 GMT the shares were up 4.90 guilders at 95.50 after hitting an early high of 96.50.</p>
<p>After the bourse closed on Thursday CSM announced the acquisition of U.S. bakery ingredients maker Karp's Inc.  </p>
<p>CSM said it would pay cash for Karp's, which has annual sales of $190 million, but it did not mention the cost of the purchase.</p>
<p>&quot;People like the CSM story,&quot; one Amsterdam share trader said of the deal.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
